WEBVTT

00:00:08.023 --> 00:00:09.454
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:09.772 --> 00:00:10.658
Sammy!

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:13.635
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can! Go!

00:00:17.632 --> 00:00:18.655
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:20.722
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:25.817
This is dad's book.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.617
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:29.775
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:29.844 --> 00:00:30.957
Family business.

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:32.502
Do you think Mom wanted all this for us?

00:00:32.593 --> 00:00:33.706
I can't do this alone.

00:00:34.521 --> 00:00:35.520
I'm driving.

00:01:22.766 --> 00:01:24.379
Can't keep kids out of this place.

00:01:24.629 --> 00:01:25.765
What is it anyway?

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.287
I forgot you're not a local.

00:01:27.446 --> 00:01:28.469
You don't know the legend.

00:01:28.878 --> 00:01:29.650
Legend?

00:01:29.832 --> 00:01:31.768
Every town's got its stories, right?

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.836
Ours is Roosevelt asylum.

00:01:34.518 --> 00:01:36.790
They say it's haunted with
the ghosts of the patients.

00:01:37.227 --> 00:01:38.113
Spend the night,

00:01:38.613 --> 00:01:40.340
Spirits will drive you insane.

00:01:46.859 --> 00:01:47.791
Hello?!

00:01:48.222 --> 00:01:49.313
Police officers!

00:01:52.448 --> 00:01:53.812
Police officers!

00:02:02.366 --> 00:02:04.974
You tell me these kids
brought bolt cutters?

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:06.865
Come on.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.024
Let's split up.

00:02:08.592 --> 00:02:09.523
All right.

00:02:23.724 --> 00:02:24.565
Hello?

00:02:53.516 --> 00:02:54.356
Hello?

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:18.918
All right.

00:03:19.827 --> 00:03:21.076
Come on out.

00:03:49.491 --> 00:03:50.627
Kelly, you copy?

00:03:52.694 --> 00:03:53.558
Jeez!

00:03:54.376 --> 00:03:55.443
Where the hell you been?!

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.398
In there.

00:03:56.511 --> 00:03:57.647
What was it? See anything?

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:01.677
No.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.639
This is patrol 1 4. We are
clear, we return to the station

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:31.351
Hey.

00:04:39.541 --> 00:04:40.540
So, what?

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.812
You're still not talking to me?

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:46.814
Walt.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:48.927
I said I was sorry about before.

00:04:48.972 --> 00:04:50.722
How many times do I have to say it?

00:05:11.402 --> 00:05:13.856
No, dad was in California
last we heard from him.

00:05:14.424 --> 00:05:17.128
We just thought if he
comes to you for munitions,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.019
Maybe you've seen him
in the last few weeks.

00:05:19.299 --> 00:05:21.046
Just call us if you hear anything. Okay.

00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:22.093
Thanks.

00:05:23.053 --> 00:05:24.151
Caleb hasn't heard from him?

00:05:24.201 --> 00:05:24.874
Nope.

00:05:24.999 --> 00:05:27.244
Neither has Jefferson or pastor Jim.

00:05:27.668 --> 00:05:29.215
What about the journal?
Any leads in there?

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.887
No. Same last time I looked.

00:05:30.936 --> 00:05:32.458
Nothing I can make out.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.170
I love the guy, but I swear
he writes like freaking Yoda.

00:05:36.171 --> 00:05:37.667
And maybe we should call the feds,

00:05:37.817 --> 00:05:38.865
File a missing person's out.

00:05:38.866 --> 00:05:41.260
We talked about this. Dad would be
pissed if we put the feds on his tail.

00:05:41.261 --> 00:05:42.407
I don't care anymore

00:05:42.532 --> 00:05:44.550
After all that happened back in kansas,

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:45.573
I mean...

00:05:45.823 --> 00:05:46.771
He should have been there, Dean.

00:05:46.772 --> 00:05:48.791
You said so yourself. You
tried to call him and nothing.

00:05:48.866 --> 00:05:49.864
I know.

00:05:50.311 --> 00:05:51.658
I loose my cellphone.

00:05:51.758 --> 00:05:53.604
You know, he could be
dead for all we know.

00:05:53.605 --> 00:05:54.876
Don't say that.

00:05:55.201 --> 00:05:56.723
He's not dead. He's...

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:59.118
He's what? He's hiding? He's busy?

00:06:05.579 --> 00:06:06.776
I don't believe it.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.323
What?

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:14.016
It's a-A text message.

00:06:15.213 --> 00:06:16.336
It's coordinates.

00:06:18.381 --> 00:06:20.253
You think dad was texting us?

00:06:20.449 --> 00:06:21.747
He's given us coordinates before.

00:06:21.797 --> 00:06:23.867
The man can barely work a toaster, Dean.

00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:25.439
Sam, this is good news.

00:06:25.539 --> 00:06:26.936
It means he's okay, or alive.

00:06:27.136 --> 00:06:28.757
Was there a number on the caller I.D.?

00:06:28.807 --> 00:06:30.005
Huh, it said "unknown."

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:31.332
Okay, well, where do
the coordinates point?

00:06:31.382 --> 00:06:32.655
That's the interesting part.

00:06:32.854 --> 00:06:34.301
Rockford, Illinois.

00:06:35.271 --> 00:06:36.469
Okay, and that's interesting how?

00:06:36.519 --> 00:06:39.313
I checked the local rockford
paper. Take a look at this.

00:06:42.678 --> 00:06:44.275
This cop, Walter Kelly,

00:06:44.499 --> 00:06:46.371
Comes home from his
shift, shoots his wife,

00:06:46.495 --> 00:06:48.541
Then puts the gun in his
mouth, blows his brains out.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.736
Earlier that night,
kelly and his partner

00:06:50.737 --> 00:06:53.294
Responded to a call at
the Roosevelt asylum.

00:06:53.369 --> 00:06:55.888
Okay, I'm not following. What
does this have to do with us?

00:06:55.889 --> 00:06:58.832
Dad earmarked the same
asylum in the journal.

00:06:59.603 --> 00:07:00.851
Let's see.

00:07:02.472 --> 00:07:03.171
Here.

00:07:03.246 --> 00:07:05.890
"Seven unconfirmed
sightings, two deaths"

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.487
Till last week, at least.

00:07:07.761 --> 00:07:09.556
I think this is where he wants us to go.

00:07:13.307 --> 00:07:14.429
This is a job.

00:07:16.275 --> 00:07:17.473
Dad wants us to work a job.

00:07:17.548 --> 00:07:19.244
Maybe we'll meet up with
him. Maybe he's there.

00:07:19.245 --> 00:07:20.317
Maybe he's not.

00:07:20.489 --> 00:07:22.560
May He could be sending us there
by ourselves to hunting thing.

00:07:22.561 --> 00:07:23.872
Who cares?

00:07:24.581 --> 00:07:26.477
If he wants us there,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:26.801 --> 00:07:28.523
This doesn't strike you as weird...

00:07:29.521 --> 00:07:30.494
The texting,

00:07:30.741 --> 00:07:32.013
The coordinates? Sam.

00:07:32.388 --> 00:07:34.533
Dad's telling us to go
somewhere. We're going.

00:07:55.517 --> 00:07:57.513
You're Daniel Gunderson,
right, you're cop?

00:07:57.688 --> 00:07:58.461
Yeah.

00:07:59.484 --> 00:08:00.332
I'm...

00:08:00.405 --> 00:08:01.677
Nigel Tufnel

00:08:01.727 --> 00:08:02.849
With the chicago tribune.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.396
Do you mind if I ask a couple questions

00:08:04.397 --> 00:08:05.444
About your partner?

00:08:05.445 --> 00:08:06.392
Yeah, I do.

00:08:06.393 --> 00:08:07.365
I'm just trying to have a beer here.

00:08:07.366 --> 00:08:09.685
I just want to hear
the story in your words.

00:08:10.293 --> 00:08:12.363
A week ago, my partner
was sitting in that chair,

00:08:12.762 --> 00:08:13.910
And now he's dead.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.157
Are you gonna ambush me here?

00:08:15.158 --> 00:08:15.931
Sorry,

00:08:15.932 --> 00:08:17.527
But I need to know what happened.

00:08:17.652 --> 00:08:20.421
Heyn buddy! How about leaving
the poor guy alone, huh?!

00:08:20.755 --> 00:08:23.200
The man's an officer! Why don't
you show a little respect?!

00:08:30.408 --> 00:08:31.531
You didn't have to do that.

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:32.903
Yeah, of course I did.

00:08:33.635 --> 00:08:34.932
That guy's a serious jerk.

00:08:35.157 --> 00:08:37.028
Let me buy you a beer, huh?

00:08:37.701 --> 00:08:38.699
Two?

00:08:42.317 --> 00:08:43.090
Thanks.

00:08:48.156 --> 00:08:49.603
You shoved me kind of
hard in there, buddy boy.

00:08:49.628 --> 00:08:51.125
I had to sell it, didn't I?

00:08:51.774 --> 00:08:52.971
It's method acting.

00:08:54.019 --> 00:08:54.842
Huh?

00:08:55.339 --> 00:08:56.112
Never mind.

00:08:56.113 --> 00:08:57.235
What did you find out from Gunderson?

00:08:57.335 --> 00:08:59.006
So, Walter Kelly was a good cop.

00:08:59.231 --> 00:09:00.827
Head of his class, even-Keeled.

00:09:00.877 --> 00:09:02.224
He had a bright future ahead of him.

00:09:02.225 --> 00:09:02.873
What about at home?

00:09:02.874 --> 00:09:04.842
He and his wife had a few
fights. Like everybody.

00:09:04.892 --> 00:09:06.364
But it was mostly smooth sailing.

00:09:06.514 --> 00:09:08.110
They were even talking
about having kids.

00:09:08.111 --> 00:09:10.854
All right, so how the kelly had some
deep see the crazy way in the bus

00:09:10.855 --> 00:09:12.227
Or something else did it to him. Right.

00:09:12.324 --> 00:09:14.070
What did Gunderson tell
you about the asylum?

00:09:15.193 --> 00:09:15.891
A lot.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.632
So, apparently, the cops
chased the kids here...

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:46.973
Into the south wing.

00:09:49.044 --> 00:09:50.216
South wing, huh?

00:09:50.834 --> 00:09:52.356
Wait a second.

00:09:53.579 --> 00:09:55.475
South wing, south wing.

00:09:58.493 --> 00:10:00.015
"1972,

00:10:00.215 --> 00:10:02.076
Three kids broke into the south wing.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.673
Only one survived."

00:10:03.872 --> 00:10:05.167
The way he tells it, one of his friends

00:10:05.168 --> 00:10:07.138
Went nuts and started
lighting up the place.

00:10:08.061 --> 00:10:09.707
So, whatever's going on,

00:10:09.882 --> 00:10:11.354
South wing seems like the heart of it.

00:10:11.404 --> 00:10:12.976
Yeah, but if kids are
spelunking the asylum,

00:10:12.977 --> 00:10:14.793
Why aren't there a ton more deaths?

00:10:16.789 --> 00:10:18.710
It looks like the doors
are usually chained.

00:10:19.758 --> 00:10:21.430
They could have been
chained up for years.

00:10:21.923 --> 00:10:23.670
Yeah, to keep people out.

00:10:24.318 --> 00:10:25.965
Or to keep something in.

00:10:36.319 --> 00:10:38.664
Let me know if you see any
dead people, Haley Joel.

00:10:38.814 --> 00:10:39.936
Dude, enough.

00:10:40.834 --> 00:10:42.553
I'm serious. You've got
to be careful. Right.

00:10:42.554 --> 00:10:44.748
Ghosts are attracted to
that E.S.P. Thing you got.

00:10:44.749 --> 00:10:45.946
I told you, it's not E.S.P.

00:10:45.947 --> 00:10:48.166
I just have strange vibes, sometimes,

00:10:48.765 --> 00:10:49.439
Weird dreams.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.352
Yeah, whatever. Don't ask, don't tell.

00:10:51.577 --> 00:10:52.974
Do you get any reading
on that thing or not?

00:10:53.049 --> 00:10:54.970
No. Of course, it doesn't
mean nobody's home.

00:10:55.045 --> 00:10:57.290
Spirits can't appear
during certain hours of day.

00:10:57.315 --> 00:10:58.785
The freaks come out at night.

00:10:59.009 --> 00:10:59.982
Ya. Hey Sam

00:11:00.032 --> 00:11:01.554
Who do you think is a hotter psychic

00:11:01.629 --> 00:11:03.675
Patricia Arquette,
Jennifer Love Hewitt or you?

00:11:30.648 --> 00:11:31.621
Man.

00:11:32.869 --> 00:11:34.216
Electroshock,

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:37.032
Lobotomies. They did some
twisted stuff to these people,

00:11:37.257 --> 00:11:40.175
Kind of like my man
Jack in "cuckoo's nest."

00:11:44.063 --> 00:11:45.884
So, what do you think?

00:11:46.533 --> 00:11:48.154
Ghosts are possessing people?

00:11:48.803 --> 00:11:49.676
Maybe.

00:11:50.524 --> 00:11:53.518
Maybe it's more like Amityville
or the smurl haunting.

00:11:53.714 --> 00:11:56.010
Ah, spirits driving them insane,

00:11:56.633 --> 00:11:58.779
Kind of like my man
Jack in "the shining."

00:12:02.521 --> 00:12:03.491
Dean...

00:12:05.462 --> 00:12:06.585
When are we going to talk about it?

00:12:06.685 --> 00:12:07.333
Talk about what?

00:12:07.358 --> 00:12:08.955
About the fact that dad's not here.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:11.076
Oh, uh, let's see, never.

00:12:11.077 --> 00:12:12.024
I'm being serious, man.

00:12:12.025 --> 00:12:12.851
So am I, sam.

00:12:12.852 --> 00:12:15.321
Look. He sent us here. He
obviously wants us here.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:16.643
We'll just have to pick
up the search later.

00:12:16.644 --> 00:12:18.215
It doesn't matter what he wants.

00:12:18.216 --> 00:12:20.556
See, that attitude right there,

00:12:21.055 --> 00:12:22.577
That is why I always
got the extra cookie.

00:12:22.701 --> 00:12:23.799
Dad could be in trouble.

00:12:23.874 --> 00:12:25.396
We should be looking for him.

00:12:25.421 --> 00:12:28.240
We deserve some answers, Dean. I mean,
this is our family were talking about..

00:12:28.241 --> 00:12:29.659
I understand that, sam,

00:12:29.809 --> 00:12:30.831
But he's given us an order.

00:12:30.832 --> 00:12:32.528
So what ? We've got to
always follow dad's orders?

00:12:32.553 --> 00:12:33.875
Of course we do.

00:12:44.896 --> 00:12:46.643
Sanford Ellicott

00:12:47.865 --> 00:12:48.888
You know what we got to do?

00:12:49.013 --> 00:12:51.103
We've got to find out
more about the south wing,

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.177
See if something happened here.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.778
Sam Winchester?

00:13:11.826 --> 00:13:12.575
That's me.

00:13:12.649 --> 00:13:13.647
Come on in.

00:13:19.953 --> 00:13:22.351
Thanks again for see me last minute.

00:13:37.495 --> 00:13:38.593
Dr. Ellicott?

00:13:39.413 --> 00:13:40.611
Ellicott, that name.

00:13:40.885 --> 00:13:43.929
Wasn't there a dr. Sanford Ellicott?

00:13:44.328 --> 00:13:46.947
Yeah, he was a chief
psychiatrist somewhere.

00:13:46.948 --> 00:13:49.989
My father was chief of staff
at the old Roosevelt asylum.

00:13:50.114 --> 00:13:51.162
How did you know?

00:13:51.785 --> 00:13:54.829
Huh, well, I'm sort of
a local-History buff.

00:13:54.976 --> 00:13:58.768
Hey, wasn't there an incident
or something in the...

00:13:58.968 --> 00:14:00.864
In the hospital, I guess,
in the south wing, right?

00:14:00.913 --> 00:14:02.435
We're on your dollar, Sam.

00:14:03.251 --> 00:14:04.873
We're here to talk about you.

00:14:05.796 --> 00:14:07.867
Oh, okay, yeah, yeah, sure.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:10.733
So? So.

00:14:10.858 --> 00:14:12.005
How's things?

00:14:12.205 --> 00:14:14.550
Uh, things are good, doctor.

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:15.448
Good.

00:14:15.648 --> 00:14:16.895
What you been doing?

00:14:17.741 --> 00:14:18.863
Uh...

00:14:19.487 --> 00:14:21.632
Same old. I've just been on a...

00:14:21.707 --> 00:14:23.728
On a road trip with my brother.

00:14:23.803 --> 00:14:25.025
Was that fun?

00:14:27.094 --> 00:14:28.116
Loads.

00:14:28.665 --> 00:14:29.763
Um...

00:14:30.137 --> 00:14:31.310
You know... We...

00:14:32.507 --> 00:14:33.954
Met a lot of...

00:14:34.703 --> 00:14:35.825
Interesting people.

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:36.624
Mm-Hmm.

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:38.297
Did a lot of, uh...

00:14:39.394 --> 00:14:40.991
A lot of interesting things.

00:14:41.814 --> 00:14:42.937
Uh...

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:44.958
You know,

00:14:45.332 --> 00:14:46.430
What was it...

00:14:46.494 --> 00:14:48.415
Exactly that happened in the south wing?

00:14:48.465 --> 00:14:49.413
I forget... Look,

00:14:49.563 --> 00:14:50.960
If you're a local-History buff,

00:14:51.007 --> 00:14:53.003
Then you know all about
the Roosevelt riot.

00:14:53.353 --> 00:14:54.101
The riot?

00:14:54.126 --> 00:14:56.346
Well, no, I know, I'm
just curious -- Sam.

00:14:57.095 --> 00:14:58.517
Let's cut the bull, shall we?

00:14:59.263 --> 00:15:00.760
You're avoiding the subject.

00:15:03.953 --> 00:15:04.852
What subject?

00:15:04.951 --> 00:15:05.800
You.

00:15:06.423 --> 00:15:08.020
Now, I'll make you a deal.

00:15:08.691 --> 00:15:10.886
I'll tell you all
about the Roosevelt riot

00:15:11.061 --> 00:15:13.456
If you tell me something
honest about yourself...

00:15:14.129 --> 00:15:15.152
Like, uh...

00:15:15.748 --> 00:15:17.744
This brother you're road-Tripping with.

00:15:18.243 --> 00:15:19.715
How do you feel about him?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:31.974
Dude.

00:15:32.074 --> 00:15:34.219
You were in there forever. What
the hell were you talking about?

00:15:34.566 --> 00:15:35.764
Just the hospital, you know.

00:15:35.838 --> 00:15:36.562
And?

00:15:36.637 --> 00:15:38.308
And the south wing,

00:15:38.408 --> 00:15:39.930
It's where they housed
the real hard cases,

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:41.776
Psychotics, the criminally insane.

00:15:41.823 --> 00:15:42.572
Sounds cozy.

00:15:42.597 --> 00:15:44.842
Yeah, and one night in '64, they rioted,

00:15:45.041 --> 00:15:46.962
Attacked the staff, attacked each other.

00:15:47.037 --> 00:15:48.609
So, what, the patients
took over the asylum?

00:15:48.756 --> 00:15:50.278
Apparently. Any deaths?

00:15:50.578 --> 00:15:52.524
Some patients, some staff.

00:15:52.648 --> 00:15:53.796
I guess it was pretty gory.

00:15:53.797 --> 00:15:55.542
Some of the bodies were
never even recovered,

00:15:55.642 --> 00:15:57.663
Including our chief of staff, Ellicott.

00:15:57.664 --> 00:15:58.935
What do you mean "Never recovered"?

00:15:58.963 --> 00:16:00.286
Cops scoured every inch of the place,

00:16:00.336 --> 00:16:02.207
But I guess the patients must have...

00:16:03.354 --> 00:16:05.625
Stuffed the bodies somewhere hidden.

00:16:05.996 --> 00:16:07.094
That's grim. Ya.

00:16:07.568 --> 00:16:09.738
So they transferred all
the surviving patients

00:16:09.739 --> 00:16:11.285
And shut down the hospital for good.

00:16:11.286 --> 00:16:14.275
All right so the * we've got a bunch of
violent deaths and unrecovered bodies.

00:16:14.276 --> 00:16:15.821
Which could mean a
bunch of angry spirits.

00:16:16.096 --> 00:16:18.404
Not good times. Let's check
out the hospital tonight.

00:16:39.127 --> 00:16:40.574
Check this out.

00:16:41.796 --> 00:16:42.769
Creepy...

00:16:44.571 --> 00:16:45.868
Yet terrifying.

00:16:47.739 --> 00:16:49.361
I thought we were going to a movie.

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:51.881
This is better. It's
like we're in a movie.

00:16:53.774 --> 00:16:55.545
I can't believe you call this a date.

00:16:58.436 --> 00:16:59.858
Come on. That'll be fine.

00:17:00.407 --> 00:17:01.729
That's look around.

00:17:02.328 --> 00:17:03.500
Come on!

00:17:10.461 --> 00:17:11.484
What was that? Ugh!

00:17:15.077 --> 00:17:16.075
Hey, look.

00:17:16.297 --> 00:17:17.719
Come on, let's check it out.

00:17:18.093 --> 00:17:19.540
I don't want to.

00:17:20.314 --> 00:17:21.037
Let's just go.

00:17:21.087 --> 00:17:22.359
Come on.

00:17:25.136 --> 00:17:26.059
Okay.

00:17:26.433 --> 00:17:27.656
Okay. You can wait here.

00:17:27.756 --> 00:17:29.003
Gavin, no.

00:17:29.103 --> 00:17:30.325
I'm just gonna be a minute.

00:17:31.772 --> 00:17:33.693
Nothing's gonna get you, I promise.

00:18:26.496 --> 00:18:27.469
Damn it.

00:18:31.541 --> 00:18:33.761
Hey, sweetie, couldn't take it, huh?

00:18:38.125 --> 00:18:38.998
Hey.

00:18:43.813 --> 00:18:46.033
Gavin, where are you?

00:18:48.411 --> 00:18:49.434
Gavin.

00:19:18.518 --> 00:19:19.641
Getting readings?

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.137
No, big-Time.

00:19:21.362 --> 00:19:23.358
This place is orbing like crazy.

00:19:27.347 --> 00:19:29.393
There's probably multiple
spirits out and about.

00:19:29.439 --> 00:19:31.884
And if these unrecovered
bodies are causing the haunting?

00:19:31.885 --> 00:19:33.205
We got to find them and burn them.

00:19:33.255 --> 00:19:33.986
Just be careful.

00:19:33.987 --> 00:19:36.959
The only thing that makes me more
nervous than a pissed-Off spirit

00:19:37.446 --> 00:19:40.217
Is a pissed-Off spirit
of a psycho killer.

00:20:51.166 --> 00:20:51.901
Dean!

00:20:52.636 --> 00:20:53.258
Dean!

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:54.870
Shotgun!

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:56.341
Sam, get down!

00:21:06.425 --> 00:21:07.415
That was weird.

00:21:07.613 --> 00:21:08.320
Yeah,

00:21:08.715 --> 00:21:09.592
You're telling me.

00:21:11.571 --> 00:21:14.286
No, Dean, I mean, it was weird
that she didn't attack me.

00:21:14.377 --> 00:21:16.186
It looked pretty aggro
from where I was standing.

00:21:16.187 --> 00:21:17.431
She didn't hurt me.

00:21:17.515 --> 00:21:18.703
She didn't even try.

00:21:19.105 --> 00:21:21.452
So she didn't want to hurt
me, then what did she want?

00:21:50.512 --> 00:21:51.983
It's all right.We're
not going to hurt you.

00:21:53.821 --> 00:21:54.895
It's okay.

00:21:55.778 --> 00:21:56.457
What's your name?

00:21:56.485 --> 00:21:57.277
Katherine.

00:21:58.578 --> 00:21:59.454
Kat.

00:21:59.624 --> 00:22:00.359
Okay.

00:22:00.614 --> 00:22:01.660
I'm dean.This is sam.

00:22:01.661 --> 00:22:02.904
What are you doing here?

00:22:04.215 --> 00:22:06.025
My boyfriend, Gavin...

00:22:06.308 --> 00:22:07.354
Is he here?

00:22:07.954 --> 00:22:09.057
Somewhere.

00:22:09.735 --> 00:22:12.676
He thought it would be fun,
try and see some ghosts.

00:22:13.468 --> 00:22:15.193
I thought it was all just...

00:22:16.075 --> 00:22:17.065
You know...

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:18.931
Pretend.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:23.003
I've seen things.

00:22:24.537 --> 00:22:26.431
I heard Gavin scream, and...

00:22:26.516 --> 00:22:28.184
All right, Kat, come on.

00:22:28.524 --> 00:22:30.446
Sam's gonna get you out of here.
Then we're gonna find your boyfriend.

00:22:30.464 --> 00:22:32.076
No, no.

00:22:33.179 --> 00:22:35.130
I'm not gonna leave without Gavin.

00:22:35.385 --> 00:22:36.685
I'm coming with you.

00:22:36.686 --> 00:22:38.728
It's no a joke around
here, okay. It's dangerous.

00:22:38.813 --> 00:22:40.509
That's why I've got to find him.

00:22:42.149 --> 00:22:43.846
All right, I guess we're
gonna split up, then.

00:22:44.096 --> 00:22:45.029
Let's go.

00:22:49.327 --> 00:22:50.401
Gavin!

00:22:54.000 --> 00:22:54.990
Gavin!

00:22:58.157 --> 00:22:59.118
Gavin!

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:02.738
Gavin!

00:23:03.112 --> 00:23:04.497
I've got a question for you.

00:23:04.893 --> 00:23:06.816
You've seen a lot of
horror movies, yeah?

00:23:07.042 --> 00:23:07.834
I guess so.

00:23:07.835 --> 00:23:09.700
Do me a favor. Next time you see one,

00:23:09.870 --> 00:23:10.916
Pay attention.

00:23:11.351 --> 00:23:12.963
When someone says a place is haunted,

00:23:13.246 --> 00:23:14.349
Don't go in.

00:23:29.112 --> 00:23:29.875
Gavin?

00:23:30.497 --> 00:23:31.600
Hey, gavin.

00:23:32.477 --> 00:23:34.626
Hey, it's okay. It's
okay. I'm here to help.

00:23:35.333 --> 00:23:36.039
Who are you?

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:37.375
My name is Sam.

00:23:37.884 --> 00:23:39.213
We found your girlfriend.

00:23:39.694 --> 00:23:40.571
Kat? Yeah.

00:23:40.572 --> 00:23:41.730
Is she all right?

00:23:41.934 --> 00:23:44.151
She's worried about you. Are you okay?

00:23:45.821 --> 00:23:47.484
I was running. I, uh,

00:23:47.614 --> 00:23:48.690
I think I fell.

00:23:48.691 --> 00:23:50.060
You were running from what?

00:23:51.854 --> 00:23:53.060
There was...

00:23:53.582 --> 00:23:56.328
There was this girl. Her-Her face...

00:23:57.925 --> 00:23:59.067
It was all messed up.

00:23:59.068 --> 00:24:00.110
Okay, listen, listen,

00:24:00.111 --> 00:24:02.099
This girl, did she try to hurt you?

00:24:02.726 --> 00:24:04.780
What? No, she, uh...

00:24:05.595 --> 00:24:06.867
She what?

00:24:08.041 --> 00:24:09.215
She kissed me.

00:24:11.700 --> 00:24:14.537
Um, but she didn't hurt you physically?

00:24:14.732 --> 00:24:16.656
Dude, she kissed me.

00:24:17.308 --> 00:24:18.482
I'm scarred for life.

00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:21.358
Trust me, it could have been worse.

00:24:21.359 --> 00:24:23.021
And now, do you remember anything else?

00:24:23.445 --> 00:24:24.619
She, uh...

00:24:25.467 --> 00:24:27.423
Actually, she tried to
whisper something in my ear.

00:24:28.050 --> 00:24:28.930
What?

00:24:29.745 --> 00:24:31.278
I don't know. I ran like hell.

00:24:45.991 --> 00:24:47.915
You son of a bitch.

00:24:48.697 --> 00:24:50.556
It's all right. I've got a lighter.

00:24:53.674 --> 00:24:55.663
Ow. You're hurting my arm.

00:24:56.674 --> 00:24:57.881
What are you talking about?

00:25:06.681 --> 00:25:09.355
Let me out!Please!

00:25:14.270 --> 00:25:16.433
Kat, hang on!

00:25:44.039 --> 00:25:44.985
What's going on?

00:25:44.986 --> 00:25:46.142
She's inside with one of them.

00:25:46.143 --> 00:25:47.382
Help me!

00:25:47.447 --> 00:25:48.197
Kat!

00:25:48.198 --> 00:25:49.469
Get me out of here!

00:25:49.470 --> 00:25:51.381
Kat, it's not gonna hurt you.

00:25:51.903 --> 00:25:54.544
Listen to me. You have to
face it. You have to calm down.

00:25:54.545 --> 00:25:55.693
She's got to what?

00:25:55.694 --> 00:25:56.606
I have to what?

00:25:56.607 --> 00:25:59.443
These spirits, they don't try to
hurt, they're trying to communicate.

00:25:59.444 --> 00:26:01.041
You've got to listen to.
You've got to face it.

00:26:01.042 --> 00:26:01.986
You face it.

00:26:01.987 --> 00:26:03.617
No. It's the only way you're
gonna get out of there.

00:26:03.618 --> 00:26:04.398
No!

00:26:04.399 --> 00:26:05.572
Look at it.That's all.

00:26:05.637 --> 00:26:06.974
Come on.You can do it.

00:26:28.522 --> 00:26:29.272
Kat?

00:26:31.164 --> 00:26:32.794
Now, I hope you're right about this.

00:26:34.791 --> 00:26:35.998
Yeah, me, too.

00:26:45.924 --> 00:26:47.065
Oh, Kat.

00:26:52.289 --> 00:26:53.659
1, 3, 7.

00:26:54.409 --> 00:26:55.452
Sorry?

00:26:56.789 --> 00:26:58.420
It whispered in my ear

00:26:58.811 --> 00:26:59.952
1, 3, 7.

00:27:00.937 --> 00:27:02.404
Room number.

00:27:05.698 --> 00:27:08.259
All right. So if these spirits
aren't trying to hurt anyone.

00:27:08.260 --> 00:27:09.825
Then what are they trying to do?

00:27:10.151 --> 00:27:11.423
Maybe that's what they've
been trying to tell us.

00:27:11.424 --> 00:27:12.564
I guess we'll find out.

00:27:13.249 --> 00:27:14.194
All right.

00:27:16.842 --> 00:27:17.723
So,

00:27:17.724 --> 00:27:19.940
Now, you guys ready to leave this place?

00:27:20.462 --> 00:27:21.669
That's an understatement.

00:27:21.702 --> 00:27:22.712
Okay.

00:27:23.136 --> 00:27:24.539
You get them out of here.

00:27:24.740 --> 00:27:26.469
I'm gonna gofind room 137.

00:27:35.438 --> 00:27:38.307
So, how do you guys know
about all this ghost stuff?

00:27:39.547 --> 00:27:41.405
It's kind of our job.

00:27:42.455 --> 00:27:44.412
Why would anyone want a job like that?

00:27:46.825 --> 00:27:48.944
I had a crappy guidance counselor.

00:27:51.201 --> 00:27:53.418
And Dean? He's your boss?

00:27:55.733 --> 00:27:56.614
No.

00:28:40.730 --> 00:28:41.740
All right.

00:28:42.001 --> 00:28:43.632
I think we have a small problem.

00:28:44.217 --> 00:28:45.260
Let's break it down.

00:28:45.423 --> 00:28:46.434
I don't think that's gonna work.

00:28:46.564 --> 00:28:47.445
Then a window.

00:28:47.446 --> 00:28:48.097
They're barred.

00:28:48.098 --> 00:28:49.793
How are we supposed to get out?

00:28:51.782 --> 00:28:53.510
That's the point. We're not.

00:28:54.071 --> 00:28:55.376
There's something in here.

00:28:55.506 --> 00:28:56.712
It doesn't want us to leave.

00:28:59.060 --> 00:28:59.941
Those patients.

00:29:00.006 --> 00:29:00.952
No.

00:29:01.473 --> 00:29:02.582
Something else.

00:29:28.340 --> 00:29:30.851
This is why I get paid the big bucks.

00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:38.737
"Patients journal."

00:29:54.934 --> 00:29:57.542
All work and no play makes Dr. Ellicott,

00:29:57.680 --> 00:29:59.669
A very dull boy.

00:30:07.601 --> 00:30:09.390
Right. I've looked everywhere.

00:30:09.672 --> 00:30:10.767
There's no other way out.

00:30:11.143 --> 00:30:12.128
So, what the hell are we gonna do?

00:30:12.191 --> 00:30:13.745
For starters, we're not gonna panic.

00:30:13.885 --> 00:30:14.949
Why the hell not?

00:30:17.484 --> 00:30:18.110
Hey.

00:30:18.157 --> 00:30:19.189
Sam, it's me.

00:30:19.659 --> 00:30:21.364
I see it. It's coming at me.

00:30:21.682 --> 00:30:22.401
Where are you?

00:30:22.402 --> 00:30:23.481
I'm in the basement. Hurry up!

00:30:23.512 --> 00:30:24.420
I'm on my way.

00:30:24.670 --> 00:30:26.751
All right. Can either
of you handle a shotgun?

00:30:27.158 --> 00:30:28.112
What?! No!

00:30:28.566 --> 00:30:29.270
I can.

00:30:30.980 --> 00:30:32.763
My dad took me skeet
shooting a couple times.

00:30:32.810 --> 00:30:33.655
Oh, I heard.

00:30:33.796 --> 00:30:34.828
It's loaded with rock salt.

00:30:34.875 --> 00:30:35.845
Now, it might not kill a spirit,

00:30:35.892 --> 00:30:37.394
But it will repel it,
so if you see something,

00:30:37.551 --> 00:30:38.051
Shoot.

00:30:38.067 --> 00:30:38.724
Okay.

00:30:38.959 --> 00:30:39.569
Okay.

00:30:46.286 --> 00:30:47.083
Dean!

00:31:05.655 --> 00:31:06.515
Dean!

00:32:07.622 --> 00:32:08.452
Dean?

00:32:36.013 --> 00:32:37.296
Don't be afraid.

00:32:37.640 --> 00:32:39.142
I'm going to make you all better.

00:32:46.447 --> 00:32:47.495
Hey, Gavin.

00:32:49.237 --> 00:32:49.941
Yeah?

00:32:51.677 --> 00:32:53.398
If we make it out of here alive,

00:32:54.587 --> 00:32:56.105
We are so breaking up.

00:32:59.544 --> 00:33:00.592
Did you hear that?

00:33:00.764 --> 00:33:01.828
Something's coming.

00:33:05.489 --> 00:33:06.882
Damn it! Damn it! Damn it!

00:33:07.492 --> 00:33:08.822
Don't shoot! It's me!

00:33:09.072 --> 00:33:10.735
Sorry. Sorry.

00:33:11.314 --> 00:33:12.581
Son of a...

00:33:16.915 --> 00:33:18.167
What are you still doing here?

00:33:18.438 --> 00:33:19.392
Where's Sam?

00:33:19.705 --> 00:33:21.144
He went to the basement. You called him.

00:33:21.989 --> 00:33:22.787
I didn't call him.

00:33:22.917 --> 00:33:24.043
His cellphone rang.

00:33:24.340 --> 00:33:25.295
He said it was you.

00:33:27.329 --> 00:33:28.314
Basement, huh?

00:33:32.630 --> 00:33:33.474
All right.

00:33:34.585 --> 00:33:35.571
Watch yourselves.

00:33:37.761 --> 00:33:38.856
And watch out for me.

00:33:45.080 --> 00:33:45.878
Sammy?

00:33:47.615 --> 00:33:48.866
Sam, you down here?

00:33:49.758 --> 00:33:50.572
Sam!

00:33:53.075 --> 00:33:53.971
Sam!

00:33:56.303 --> 00:33:57.038
Man...

00:33:57.820 --> 00:33:59.432
Answer me when I'm calling you.

00:33:59.995 --> 00:34:00.574
You all right?

00:34:00.575 --> 00:34:01.638
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:34:01.779 --> 00:34:03.202
You know that wasn't
me who called, right?

00:34:03.300 --> 00:34:05.286
Yeah, I know. I think
something lured me down here.

00:34:05.287 --> 00:34:06.648
I think I know who

00:34:06.867 --> 00:34:07.727
Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:08.169 --> 00:34:10.375
That's what the spirits have been trying
to tell us. You haven't seen him, have you?

00:34:10.469 --> 00:34:11.283
No.

00:34:11.471 --> 00:34:12.425
How do you knowit was him?

00:34:12.426 --> 00:34:13.770
Because I found his logbook.

00:34:13.802 --> 00:34:16.336
Apparently, he was
experimenting on his patients.

00:34:16.826 --> 00:34:17.952
Awful stuff.

00:34:17.983 --> 00:34:19.658
Makes lobotomies look
like a couple of aspirin.

00:34:19.659 --> 00:34:21.300
But it was the patients who rioted.

00:34:21.301 --> 00:34:23.053
Yeah. They were rioting
against Dr. Ellicott.

00:34:24.304 --> 00:34:27.782
Dr. Feelgood was working on some
sort of extreme-Rage therapy.

00:34:27.783 --> 00:34:30.113
He thought if he could get his
patients to vent their anger,

00:34:30.223 --> 00:34:31.506
Then they'd be cured of it.

00:34:31.897 --> 00:34:33.196
Instead it only made
them worse and worse

00:34:33.197 --> 00:34:34.447
And angrier and angrier.

00:34:34.651 --> 00:34:36.090
I'm thinking, what if his spirit

00:34:36.309 --> 00:34:37.529
Is doing the same thing?

00:34:37.764 --> 00:34:38.531
To the cop,

00:34:38.645 --> 00:34:40.022
The kids in the '70s

00:34:40.335 --> 00:34:42.697
Making them so angry
they become homicidal.

00:34:43.777 --> 00:34:44.449
Come on.

00:34:44.731 --> 00:34:46.421
We've got to find his
bones and torch them.

00:34:46.921 --> 00:34:47.766
How?

00:34:48.086 --> 00:34:49.400
The police never found his body.

00:34:49.462 --> 00:34:52.185
The logbook said he had some
hidden procedure room down here

00:34:52.186 --> 00:34:54.328
Somewhere where he'd
work on his patients. So,

00:34:54.474 --> 00:34:56.273
If I was a patient, I'd
drag his ass down here

00:34:56.274 --> 00:34:57.634
Do a little work on myself.

00:34:57.681 --> 00:34:59.089
I don't know.It sounds kind of...

00:34:59.152 --> 00:34:59.871
Of crazy?

00:34:59.872 --> 00:35:00.387
Yeah.

00:35:00.388 --> 00:35:01.858
Yeah, exactly.

00:35:17.858 --> 00:35:19.110
I told you I looked everywhere.

00:35:19.111 --> 00:35:20.815
I didn't find a hidden room.

00:35:21.191 --> 00:35:22.771
Well, that's why they call it hidden.

00:35:25.701 --> 00:35:26.765
You hear that?

00:35:28.204 --> 00:35:29.112
What?

00:35:39.978 --> 00:35:41.229
There's a door here.

00:35:44.609 --> 00:35:45.532
Dean.

00:35:50.938 --> 00:35:52.518
Step back from the door.

00:35:57.472 --> 00:35:58.818
Sam, put the gun down.

00:35:59.193 --> 00:36:00.351
Is that an order?

00:36:02.025 --> 00:36:03.699
That's more of a friendly request.

00:36:03.700 --> 00:36:05.999
'Cause I'm getting pretty
tired of taking your orders.

00:36:07.631 --> 00:36:08.726
I knew it.

00:36:09.321 --> 00:36:10.479
Ellicott did something
to you, didn't he?

00:36:10.480 --> 00:36:11.699
For once in your life,

00:36:12.122 --> 00:36:13.029
Shut your mouth.

00:36:13.030 --> 00:36:14.427
What are you gonna do, sam?

00:36:14.953 --> 00:36:16.696
The gun's filled with rock salt.

00:36:16.888 --> 00:36:17.920
It's not gonna kill me.

00:36:21.284 --> 00:36:21.910
No.

00:36:22.207 --> 00:36:23.115
But it'll hurt like hell.

00:36:31.108 --> 00:36:31.906
Sam.

00:36:32.531 --> 00:36:34.112
We've got to burn Ellicott's bones,

00:36:34.143 --> 00:36:35.520
And all this will be over,

00:36:35.885 --> 00:36:37.105
And you'll be back to normal.

00:36:37.277 --> 00:36:38.325
I am normal.

00:36:39.358 --> 00:36:40.969
I'm just telling the
truth for the first time.

00:36:41.470 --> 00:36:43.191
I mean, why are we even here?

00:36:43.989 --> 00:36:46.685
'Cause you're following dad's
orders like a good little soldier?

00:36:46.779 --> 00:36:49.297
'Cause you always do what
he says without question?

00:36:49.595 --> 00:36:51.597
Are you that desperate for his approval?

00:36:51.801 --> 00:36:53.240
This isn't you talking, Sam.

00:36:53.308 --> 00:36:54.904
That's the difference
between you and me.

00:36:55.123 --> 00:36:57.000
I have a mind of my own.

00:36:57.250 --> 00:36:59.018
I'm not pathetic like you.

00:36:59.019 --> 00:37:01.099
So what are you gonna do?
Huh. You gonna kill me?

00:37:01.146 --> 00:37:04.072
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:01.146 --> 00:37:04.072
You know, I am sick of
doing what you tell me to do.

00:37:04.562 --> 00:37:06.456
We're no closer to finding dad today

00:37:06.564 --> 00:37:08.395
Than we were six months ago.

00:37:10.277 --> 00:37:11.560
Well, then here.

00:37:11.810 --> 00:37:13.641
Let me make it easier for you.

00:37:15.831 --> 00:37:16.801
Come on.

00:37:16.989 --> 00:37:17.943
Take it.

00:37:18.297 --> 00:37:21.144
Real bullets are gonna work a hell
of a lot better than rock salt.

00:37:22.208 --> 00:37:23.100
Take it.

00:37:34.981 --> 00:37:36.483
You hate me that much?

00:37:38.110 --> 00:37:39.941
You think you can kill your own brother?

00:37:42.819 --> 00:37:44.164
Then go ahead.

00:37:45.385 --> 00:37:46.652
Pull the trigger.

00:37:53.011 --> 00:37:54.231
Do it!

00:38:11.773 --> 00:38:14.120
Man, I'm not gonna give
you a loaded pistol.

00:38:21.597 --> 00:38:22.833
Sorry, Sammy.

00:39:26.269 --> 00:39:27.739
Oh, that's just gross.

00:39:36.804 --> 00:39:37.884
Soak it up.

00:39:50.761 --> 00:39:52.170
Don't be afraid.

00:39:53.003 --> 00:39:54.396
I'm going to help you.

00:39:54.505 --> 00:39:56.336
I'm going to make you all better.

00:40:47.524 --> 00:40:49.386
You're not gonna try
and kill me, are you?

00:40:52.296 --> 00:40:53.125
No.

00:40:53.959 --> 00:40:54.815
Good.

00:40:56.196 --> 00:40:58.152
'Cause that would be awkward.

00:41:04.350 --> 00:41:05.492
Thanks, guys.

00:41:05.821 --> 00:41:07.010
Yeah, thanks.

00:41:07.401 --> 00:41:09.466
No more haunted asylums, okay?

00:41:16.894 --> 00:41:17.864
Hey, Dean.

00:41:19.256 --> 00:41:20.837
I' sorry, man. I

00:41:22.088 --> 00:41:23.950
said some awful thingsback there.

00:41:24.518 --> 00:41:25.785
You remember all that?

00:41:26.176 --> 00:41:27.037
Yeah.

00:41:28.727 --> 00:41:31.605
It's like I couldn't control
it, but I didn't mean it

00:41:32.012 --> 00:41:32.982
Any of it.

00:41:33.671 --> 00:41:34.625
You didn't, huh?

00:41:35.647 --> 00:41:36.664
No. Of course, not.

00:41:39.532 --> 00:41:41.112
Do we need to talk about this?

00:41:42.129 --> 00:41:43.005
No.

00:41:43.091 --> 00:41:45.868
I'm not really in the sharing
and caring kind of mood.

00:41:46.474 --> 00:41:48.023
I just want to get some sleep.

00:42:03.337 --> 00:42:04.197
Dean.

00:42:11.835 --> 00:42:12.695
Hello.

00:42:15.699 --> 00:42:16.419
Dad?



00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.000
